WEBVTT

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.430
It’s been four years, hasn’t it?

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.350
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.180
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.520
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.880
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.200
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.410
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:23.020
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:30.990
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:38.870
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:46.580
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:54.050
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:03.430
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:12.190
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.450
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.450
is the light of only you.

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:23.190
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:28.040
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:35.720
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.500
With a little prayer!!

00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.590
An oath on the grave!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:48.400
From the Southern Tokyo Branch: Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:52.070
From the Sugaru Branch:
Umino Katsuo.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:57.690
We’ll now begin the third examination for the B block,

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.110
that is, the quarterfinals match.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:01.780
Begin!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.370
All right!

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.580
Katsuo!
Hang in there!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:13.590
Fight! Fight!

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:16.340
Okay! I definitely won’t lose!

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.120
T-This is definitely not
what you’d expect...

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.760
To think that such a cute girl would
come to cheer Katsuo on...

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.300
However, I now have...

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.420
Good luck, Kawachi!

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.930
A good companion and rival, Azuma;

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.270
a dependable Manager;

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.640
and the level-headed high school student who acts as

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.400
the stand-in manager, Tsukino.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:42.490
Tsukino’s not there!

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.740
Manager! Where’s the little miss?

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.190
Tsukino, eh?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.860
She said that she wouldn’t come today.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.960
Apparently, there’s something
important that she had to do today.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.170
Something important?

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:55.240
When she says that it’s
“something important,”

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:58.920
does that mean it’s more important
than my match today?

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.970
I haven’t been there for a long time.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:10.680
However, I’m sure I’ll be forgiven.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.940
Because... that person is very kind.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:24.480
What is it?

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.910
A thing that’s more important than my match?

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.990
It’s probably a guy.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.700
What?!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.170
Whatever... Either way, I was...

00:04:35.660 --> 00:04:38.330
Nobody was expecting anything great out
of me from the very beginning, either way...

00:04:38.330 --> 00:04:40.710
In the end, I’m just an extra, compared to Azuma...

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.420
That’s not the case.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:52.090
So, what is it you’re trying to pull here...?

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.980
No, handicrafts are just a hobby of mine...

00:04:54.430 --> 00:04:56.850
Is he trying to comfort me or something?

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.640
Listen up, Kawachi.

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:02.610
Tsukino didn’t decide not to come today to slight you.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:04.480
It’s because she believes in you.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:06.740
She’s sure that you’ll win!

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.990
What?!

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.620
Was that what it was?

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.500
In that case,
I must answer to her expectations...

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:20.750
All right! Let’s do this!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.050
Exactly! Good luck Kawachi!

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.420
What a simple-minded fellow...

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.090
Let’s do this.

00:05:30.090 --> 00:05:32.440
I have many people firmly on my side.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:43.190
It’s nice to see that the idiots over
there are having a good time, right?

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.950
Yeah, they’re people that make you feel good.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.450
You’re from the B block...?

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.150
I’m Kanmuri Shigeru.

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:54.660
Nice to meet you.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.250
From the Central Shinjuku Branch, right?

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:00.210
I’ve heard about you from Kuroyanagi.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.210
Not surprisingly, that man has always
been a gossip, hasn’t he?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:06.920
But, oh well...

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.130
It’s an honor to think that the
person considered to be the strongest here

00:06:10.130 --> 00:06:12.930
in the newcomers’ battle, Suwabara-san, knows me.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.590
Enough with the tedious talk!

00:06:14.590 --> 00:06:17.430
Moreover, aren’t you supposed
to be in a match right now?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.440
What in the world do you want from me?

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:20.760
Oh, my...

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:23.940
Please don’t make such a scary face.

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:26.690
I was making no such thing...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.860
I just came by to say hello.

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:32.450
And just like you, I also have...

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.950
a default win.

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.780
Isn’t it strange?

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:41.790
As a symbol of friendship, I usually
present my opponent with

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.840
my bread for a taste before the match,

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:47.920
but for some reason,

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.430
after they eat it, everybody retires from
the match as though they are avoiding me.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.480
Honestly... Adults these days are really not up to mark.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.730
That man over there, competing in B block...

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.480
Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:11.200
Even you will no longer be able to
speak like this, after meeting him.

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:15.030
That’s some sort of joke, right?

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:19.200
If you say it with such a scary
face, you might get taken seriously...

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.830
I do not joke.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.710
And this is a normal face!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.880
I give this to you as a symbol of our friendship.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.220
All right, then. I’m off...

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:33.390
I don’t like this person.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:34.720
But...

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:40.770
To make bread that stimulates my palate so much...

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.730
He’s definitely something out of the ordinary!

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.570
I’m done!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.200
Me, too!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:55.990
Kawachi has a simple crab, eh?

00:07:55.990 --> 00:08:00.700
He’s just trying for the Dotombori-crab look because he’s from Osaka, eh?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:05.200
Since I had such high expectations,
I’m even more disappointed.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.660
Boring...

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.410
Compared to...

00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:11.470
Umino’s animal-bread that I
hadn’t really been expecting much of...

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.930
This is...

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.340
a person.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:19.380
The idea of classifying humans
as animals is pretty unique.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.430
And it is somewhat cute...

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.100
Hey, the pig over there.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.760
What is this?

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.940
It’s my “Momma.”

00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:31.690
That rather beautiful person is...

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.520
your mother, Katsuo?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.150
There’s a limit to your being able to say,
“She looks rather young for her age.”

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:41.250
And by the way, how old was she when she had you?

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.960
What are you blabbing, Kuroyanagi-san?

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.750
That’s my Momma. My wife.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.710
Darling!

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:52.920
What?!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:54.180
What?!

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:57.000
What was that?

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:57.890
Impossible!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.050
You... How old are you?

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.810
I’m 31.

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.060
You’re older than me?!

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.190
It’s not possible!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.310
He’s the same age as me!

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:11.440
He’s twice as old as me!

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:13.570
Tsukino’s a high school student.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.950
How much of that is true?

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:17.360
All of it.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:20.440
When I just joined the Sugaru Branch,

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.450
Sa-chan was a part-timer there.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.710
You’re so forceful, Katsuo...

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:28.410
We got married after three months.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:31.000
Sa-chan likes my bread, and so...

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.880
If I were to win the Pantasia newcomers’ battle,

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:39.470
then she said that she’d do this and that...

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.930
You got married while working part time?!

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.640
That’s too short a time!

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:44.850
You’re fired!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.860
I shouldn’t have helped him!

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.360
That’s so impure...

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.600
Oh, Katsuo, sweetie.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.890
That’s true, but it was a secret...

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:54.860
Is that so?
That’s true, but it was a secret...

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:55.560
Is that so?

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.360
Sa-chan!

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:00.860
You’re so quick with your hands.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:01.740
But, let’s stop at that...

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:04.410
This is what you should be looking
forward to after you win...

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.870
Just one...

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.920
Victor: Kawachi Kyousuke.

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:14.040
Wait just one moment!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.220
You haven’t even done the grading yet!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.250
Y-Yeah, Kuro-yan.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:21.220
Don’t be getting all hot and bothered.
The judging should at least be done properly.

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:27.220
Hey, why’s Kawachi complaining even though he won?

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:32.230
He’s probably got some trick to that crab-bread that he wanted him to see, at any cost.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:36.860
I haven’t lost my calm while making this decision.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:37.740
Look!

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:42.530
Dave-sensei has already graded
it as -500 points worth.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.740
He doesn’t even seem to have been able to scream.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.990
There’s no possibility here of any more tasting.

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:48.000
You´ve lost!

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.000
This is some gourmet battle...

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.000
You have no right to say that!

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:59.010
Thanks to that moron, I couldn’t
demonstrate this “moving crab-bread”...

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.510
This, here...

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:05.260
is a chiffon cake with three times
the flexibility of sponge cake...

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.640
and if you press it...

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:09.430
it moves!

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:11.480
It’s cute, right?

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:16.310
You see?

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.530
I feel kinda sorry for Kawachi.

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:20.860
Come on...

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:30.320
Boy, has Suwabara-san overestimated him...

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:31.450
Man...

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:33.490
That was a really low level fight there.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:37.500
Do I really have to fight with
everything I have against such folk?

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.420
Of course.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.710
No matter how clean a kitchen is...

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:45.260
cockroaches somehow find their way in.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:47.970
The present favorite, Mizuno, couldn’t

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:50.560
stop even one of them,

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.060
so you can take care of them all.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.640
Oh man...

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:58.560
You really work us hard, don’t you...

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:00.110
Miss Yukino.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.070
That person really loved these flowers.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.200
The person that I really loved.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.480
Well then, I will now announce the finalists,

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:19.560
the best four of the Pantasia newcomers.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:20.440
From A block:

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.520
Azuma Kazuma of the
Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.730
Hey, Azuma,

00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:27.110
this crab bread can move...

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.650
And his opponent from the Main Store, Suwabara Kai.

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:32.450
See, see, Suwabara-chan,

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:33.780
try pressing it here!

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:36.370
It really moves in a cute matter.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:37.420
You’re an embarrassment.

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.420
And from the B block:

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:42.800
Kanmuri Shigeru of the
Central Shinjuku Branch.

00:13:43.170 --> 00:13:44.880
You’re Kanmuri-kun, eh?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.760
Just try pressing it here.
It moves really well.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:51.140
Really. It’s very cute, isn’t it?

00:13:51.590 --> 00:13:55.480
His opponent is Kawachi Kyousuke
of the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.810
Hey, Kuro-yan,
it’s amazing, isn’t it?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:00.650
Please give me a proper reaction.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:03.150
Annoying!

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:08.950
Okay, a crab.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.530
Does this satisfy you?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.990
It... it was tiny.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.860
As for the schedule...

00:14:14.860 --> 00:14:17.830
we will have both the A and B
groups together in three days.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:22.120
The B block match starts at 9 a.m.,
and the A block match will start from 1 p.m.

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:23.000
The theme will be...

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:26.710
your choice.

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:28.010
Our choice?

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.840
That’s right. Your choice.

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.760
You can make any bread.

00:14:32.090 --> 00:14:32.970
But...

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:36.680
we expect you to make a
masterpiece to the best of your abilities.

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:40.180
Furthermore, from the semifinals onward, in addition to the owner Azusagawa,

00:14:40.180 --> 00:14:43.400
the General Manager, Meister
Kirisaki, will also be coming to watch.

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.100
Don’t even think of being late.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:48.240
Make sure that you don’t do anything rude.

00:14:50.770 --> 00:14:52.900
Old ma... I mean, Mr. Kuroyanagi’s really rude.

00:14:52.900 --> 00:14:56.080
Opening the door with his legs like that...

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:59.710
Kuroyanagi-senpai probably just couldn’t use his hands.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.710
My hands...

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:12.590
Kawachi’s crab-bread is fearsome.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:15.010
Because of that bread...

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.140
I won’t be able to play rock-paper-scissors for a while.

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:22.020
Crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab, crab...

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.610
I’m... I’m no good anymore...

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.730
Cheer up, Kawachi.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:33.150
Kawachi-san, it was an amazing bread.

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:38.250
Yeah. Old man Kuroyanagi was still
a crab on the other side of the door.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:39.620
Really?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.990
Of course.

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:43.630
So, cheer up, and let’s work hard. Both of us.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.170
Kanmuri-kun...

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:55.510
See you in three days.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.970
Let’s fight it out fair and square.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:58.970
Okay!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.480
He seems like a nice guy.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:04.480
I wonder if that’s really true...

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.850
He must have become afraid after seeing

00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:13.320
my strength, and it may’ve been
a plan to get into my good graces.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.490
Oh?

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:15.990
That’s amazing, Kawachi.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:16.780
How’s that?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:17.780
I’m amazing, right?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:18.200
Just what we’d expect of you, Kawachi.

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:19.410
I’m awesome, right?

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.070
You’re awesome, Kawachi.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:21.030
Right? More, more!

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.500
Kawachi.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.270
Mother.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:34.510
I’ll be there soon.

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:50.690
I really hate the smell of cigarette smoke.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:53.310
Helping the enemy out like that...

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.520
What could you be thinking?

00:16:55.520 --> 00:16:57.860
Well, I must have him try his best,

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.900
because even I need to be able to give it my all...

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:01.290
Shut up, boy!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:03.820
It’s not enough to just win.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.450
We must have the cockroaches of the

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:09.290
Southern Tokyo Branch shamed and crushed

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:11.250
in front of the owner before they leave.

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.260
Okay, okay. I understand,

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:17.390
Miss Yukino.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:25.050
You’re amazing, Kawachi!

00:17:25.050 --> 00:17:26.850
Your crab-bread is the best!

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:28.850
Say more, say more!

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:30.320
You’re amazing, Kawachi!

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.230
You’re the Kawachi amongst Kawachis!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:34.030
Obviously.

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:35.310
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:17:35.310 --> 00:17:36.320
By the way, Manager,

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.360
what was it that Tsukino had to do today?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.530
Oh yeah, that’s right.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:42.540
Why do you want to know?

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.200
Well... there’s three days before the next match.

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.120
With both of us making it to the best
four, I thought that at least for today,

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.460
all four of us from the Southern Tokyo Branch could

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:54.750
party big time!

00:17:54.750 --> 00:17:56.050
That sounds like fun.

00:17:57.460 --> 00:17:58.750
What could it be...?

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.560
I have goose bumps.

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.630
Then, let’s go see...

00:18:02.630 --> 00:18:03.810
Where?

00:18:04.260 --> 00:18:06.060
To where Tsukino is.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:18.440
It’s a graveyard. So, we’re going to visit a grave?

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.070
But whose?

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.610
Today is the anniversary of Tsukino’s mother’s death.

00:18:23.610 --> 00:18:25.080
What?

00:18:27.280 --> 00:18:30.410
Tsukino’s mother was originally a baker with the ability

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:35.210
to have become the General
Manager of Pantasia’s Main Branch.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.420
At that time, Tsukino’s father

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.250
was aiming to be a baker, and
polishing his skills at the Main Branch.

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:42.010
Azusagawa Sadamichi was...

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:44.720
captivated, and they
fell in love at first sight.

00:18:45.340 --> 00:18:48.310
Then, Tsukino was born, but...

00:18:56.850 --> 00:19:00.740
Today, four years ago, she passed away.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:15.590
We’re here.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.380
It’s an amazing grave.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:24.470
It’s really extravagant.

00:19:24.470 --> 00:19:25.930
It’s a shameful grave, isn’t it?

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:29.480
What are you saying?

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:43.320
It’s a tree. And a withered one, at that.

00:19:43.320 --> 00:19:45.150
Why is she praying there?

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:46.490
Tsukino...

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.870
That withered tree is...

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.500
Tsukino’s mother’s gravestone.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.490
What?

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:55.000
What do you mean?

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:58.000
After Tsukino’s mother’s funeral service was over,

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.010
while laying her ashes
to rest at the grave...

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.140
Stop!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.640
Give me back my mother!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.890
In the story of Old Man Hanasaka,

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:15.470
if you scatter a dog’s bones,
the cherry trees will blossom, right?

00:20:15.470 --> 00:20:19.150
I wonder what’ll blossom with the thieving cat’s bones?!

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.660
Please, stop! Miss Yukino!

00:20:24.230 --> 00:20:24.650
Here you go!

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:25.570
Mother is...

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:26.530
Here you go!

00:20:26.530 --> 00:20:27.580
Mother is...

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:34.920
No!

00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.500
I understand you getting angry.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.180
But, calm yourselves.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:48.180
Yukino is not like Mizuno.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:51.550
Yukino’s really a scary woman.

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.020
She won’t back off from any means to win.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.100
That Kanmuri Shigeru of the Central Shinjuku Branch

00:20:57.100 --> 00:21:00.190
has won by forfeits three times in a row.

00:21:00.520 --> 00:21:02.860
He’s probably quite an expert,

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.950
hired specifically for the newcomers’ battle.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:14.990
I will definitely defeat Kanmuri!

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:16.740
Absolutely and completely defeat him.

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:18.950
I won’t forgive you if you lose.

00:21:18.950 --> 00:21:20.000
You understand?

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:21.340
Of course!

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:25.000
The finals will be Southern
Tokyo vs. Southern Tokyo, okay?

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.010
It’s decided.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:03.460
You see, Mother?

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:05.880
It’s these people.

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:10.510
These people are my dear friends.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:12.930
So...

00:22:15.140 --> 00:22:15.890
Mother...

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:20.900
I’m not lonely.

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:57.210
On this chest, big and strong

00:22:57.210 --> 00:22:59.330
A look that glitters and doesn't lose.

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:01.330
That's what I searched for, fumbling in the wind.

00:23:01.330 --> 00:23:02.630
The answer for now is...

00:23:02.630 --> 00:23:05.550
For now, I'll watch the situation and wait for a chance.
I got the patience to wait at a distance.

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:07.340
A prisoner who just screams is no good.

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:09.130
Just Follow Me! I'll lend you my shoulder occasionally.

00:23:17.980 --> 00:23:19.230
It's by no means a fleeting dream.

00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:22.110
Let this sentiment reach you. Heart to Heart, Soul to Soul.

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:24.150
The seasons turn. Splendid as a spring storm.

00:23:24.150 --> 00:23:25.560
Win Big is the motto.

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:30.360
Does a thing like eternity really exist?

00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:32.200
And so we... C'mon.

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:37.750
Yeah, yeah, we live to touch the one shining moment.

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:59.470
To all the soldiers fighting today using the tail wind...

00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:08.540
I definitely won’t lose,
for Tsukino’s sake, too!

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:10.710
All right, come!
I’ll beat you to a pulp.

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:11.920
Bring it on, quickly!

00:24:11.920 --> 00:24:13.340
Let’s do this together!

00:24:13.340 --> 00:24:15.480
Man, that really takes the wind out of your sails.

00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:16.760
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:16.760 --> 00:24:18.180
The nightmarish semifinals.

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:19.590
Yukino’s despicable trap.

00:24:19.590 --> 00:24:20.930
Be sure to watch!

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:23.690
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:25.890
The chiffon cake that Kawachi
used for the crab-bread...

00:24:25.890 --> 00:24:27.640
uses vegetable oil instead of butter.

00:24:27.640 --> 00:24:30.190
The low calorie, non-cholesterol vegetable oil

00:24:30.190 --> 00:24:32.700
gives rise to that soft, fluffy dough.

00:24:32.700 --> 00:24:34.240
Is that so...?
